#   lib/caps.sh      fails OPEN: byte-identical content gives tripped=1 on LF
#     and tripped=0 on CRLF. ops-stop-hook.sh SOURCES this lib, so a CRLF
#     checkout silently disables the same-target-rework cap while every gate
#     reports green. Pre-existing on main.
#   ops-verdict.sh   --reconcile DROPS the row: "skipping non-conformant line",
#     1 of 2 restored, the CRLF row absent from the rebuilt ledger. Data loss
#     in the RECOVERY path. Pre-existing on main.
# One-line fix in each: `row="${row%$'\r'}"` before any comparison. The cases
# assert EQUALITY between the two encodings plus a control that the LF side
# actually did something — equality alone passes if both sides report zero.
# Mutation: strip the guard from all three -> 5 of 6 red (the sixth is the
# --reconcile LF control, which correctly holds either way).
#
# #137 arm 3 passed a REAL tests/ deletion it could not see. Both ls-tree
# redirects were unchecked and the loop iterates the BASE listing, so an empty
# file made it a no-op. THE TRIGGER IS A NESTED SUBTREE under tests/: a missing
# `tests/sub` tree leaves `git show BASE:tests/floors.env` working (so every
# earlier check passes) while `ls-tree -r -- tests/` must recurse and fails.
# Corrupting `scripts/` or `docs/` does NOT reach it — the base-readable check
# dies first, or git prunes the walk by pathspec. Both measured, and both were
# my first two attempts at reproducing it; the review's claim looked
# unreproducible until the right subtree was found.
# With both guards removed, 3/3 deterministic: rc 0, BASE_GATE_PASSED, zero
# GONE lines, `D tests/zzz.sh` printed by the delta report one line above.
# Mutation: remove both guards -> both #137 cases red.
#
# DECLARED UNPINNED: the `[ -n "$BASE_SHA" ]` guard added beside it has NO
# case. Removing it leaves the suite green (measured). Its trigger is a ref
# deleted or repacked BETWEEN the two rev-parse calls — a race, not an input,
# and this repo does not ship fixtures it cannot construct (the #133 rule).
# The guard is two lines and fails closed; it is recorded here rather than
# left to read as covered.
# Named per #111 rather than written up as "mutation-checked".

